<!-- field: overview -->
## Overview

The platform records agent runs, grades them, and publishes scorecards. An interface, a component, and a decision are each a node under their section; the headings below show the form each takes.

<!-- field: interfaces -->
## Interfaces

<!-- interface: run_records -->
### run_records

Each agent run, written by the agents' runtime as one record per run. An interface's heading is its id alone: the id is its name.

<!-- field: components -->
## Components

<!-- component: grader -->
### grader

Scores each run record against the agent's rubric. A component's heading is its id alone, like an interface's.

<!-- field: capabilities -->
#### Capabilities

- score: one score per run record, against the rubric the agent names

<!-- field: ownership -->
#### Ownership

- the rubrics and the scores

<!-- field: design_decisions -->
## Design decisions

<!-- decision: 1 -->
### 1 - Grade after the run, never during it

A decision's id is a number, so its heading is the number, " - ", and a title. Grading reads finished run records, so an agent's latency never depends on the grader.

<!-- field: alternatives_rejected -->
#### Alternatives rejected

- Grading inline: it would put the grader on every agent's critical path.

<!-- field: technology_choices -->
## Technology choices

| component | technology | purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| grader | a batch job | scores the day's run records |

<!-- field: project_structure -->
## Project structure

The grader lives in the evaluation repository; the run records' schema lives in the platform repository.

<!-- field: implementation_status -->
## Implementation status

The run records are written; the grader is next.

